---

<BaseLayout
  title="Rho: A Foundation for Efficiently Adaptable VLA Models"
  description="Rho is a family of open-weights, 5B-parameter vision-language-action models for bimanual robotic manipulation, built for data-efficient adaptation to new robots and tasks."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container container--wide">
      <h1>Rho</h1>
      <p class="hero__title-expansion">A Foundation for Efficiently Adaptable VLA Models</p>
      <div class="authors">
        <p class="authors__team">Rho team<sup><a href="#author-note" aria-label="Author order note">1</a></sup></p>
        <p class="authors__names">
          {authorLines.map((line, lineIndex) => (
            <span class="authors__line">
              {line.map((author, i) => (
                <Fragment>
                  <span class="authors__name">
                    {author.name}
                    {author.marks && (
                      <sup title={describeMarks(author.marks)}>
                        <span aria-hidden="true">{author.marks}</span>
                        <span class="visually-hidden">({describeMarks(author.marks)})</span>
                      </sup>
                    )}
                    {(i < line.length - 1 || lineIndex < authorLines.length - 1) && ","}
                  </span>{" "}
                </Fragment>
              ))}
            </span>
          ))}
        </p>
        <p class="authors__affiliation">Microsoft Research</p>
        <p class="authors__legend">
          <span>Area leads:</span>
          <span class="authors__legend-items">
            <span><sup>∗</sup>Data</span>
            <span><sup>§</sup>Training</span>
            <span><sup>‡</sup>Engineering</span>
            <span><sup>†</sup>VLM</span>
          </span>
          <span class="authors__legend-break"><sup>♠</sup>Project lead</span>
        </p>
        <p class="authors__note" id="author-note"><sup>1</sup>Authors are listed alphabetically.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="hero__dek">
        Rho is a family of open-weights, 5B-parameter vision-language-action
        models for bimanual robotic manipulation, designed for data-light
        adaptation. One foundation model, Rho-base, is <em>midtrained</em> into
        ready-to-adapt variants for three common dual-arm robots — YAM Box,
        UR AI Trainer, and FR3 Duo — and a task policy derived from any of them
        can keep improving after deployment from a handful of human corrections.
      </p>
      <div class="hero__links">
        {resources.map((resource) => (
          <a class="button" href={resource.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            {resource.label}<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
      <dl class="hero__stats">
        <div><dt>Model size</dt><dd>5B params</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Robot-ready variants</dt><dd>3 embodiments</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Pretraining data</dt><dd>3,200+ hours</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="variants-band" aria-labelledby="variants-title">
    <div class="container hero__variants">
      <p class="section-kicker variants-band__title" id="variants-title">Midtrained Rho variants for…</p>
      <div class="hero__media hero__media--sizzle">
        {embodiments.map((robot) => (
          <article class="variant-card">
            <video
              src={withBase(robot.reel)}
              aria-label={`${robot.name} highlight reel`}
              controls autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"
            ></video>
            <div class="variant-card__body">
              <span class="badge">{robot.maker}</span>
              <h3>{robot.name}</h3>
              <p>{robot.role}</p>
              <a href={robot.checkpoint}>Get {robot.slug} ↗</a>
            </div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="Page sections">
    <div class="container container--wide">
      <span class="section-nav__row">
        <a href="#overview">Overview</a>
